{
  "id": "12-worker-goes-down",
  "chapter": "Async",
  "title": "A Worker goes down",
  "brief": "Eight uploads arrive every second, and 10 seconds into the wave one of your Workers crashes. Nothing is lost: the Messages stay in the queue and the other Workers keep taking them. This is at-least-once delivery. The price is that a job a Worker was processing when it crashed will be delivered again, so a job may run twice, and real Workers must be idempotent: running a job twice must give the same result as running it once. Do you have enough Workers for a bad day?",
